* gf180-antifuse sim/program-read-legs: corner preamble.
*
* klt sim emits its `.lib` cards BEFORE the netlist body's `.include`s, but
* the gf180mcu model files read global parameters (fnoicor, sw_stat_global,
* ...) that design.ngspice defines, and ngspice resolves them in file order.
* A corners.process bundle is the only seam klt gives for a card ahead of
* the model sections, so design.ngspice is pulled in as the FIRST section of
* every bundle, through this one-section wrapper.
.lib design
.include $PDK_ROOT/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/ngspice/design.ngspice
.endl design

* Mismatch variant (Monte Carlo benches): the same globals, then the PDK's
* per-instance mismatch switch (sw_stat_mismatch, default 0) turned ON. Global
* process variation (sw_stat_global) stays 0, so a monte_carlo vary="mismatch"
* request samples intra-die mismatch only, on top of the named PVT corner.
.lib design_mm
.include $PDK_ROOT/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/ngspice/design.ngspice
.param sw_stat_mismatch=1
.endl design_mm
